  "pack.description": "ARCHAEOLOGY Add-On Resources Made by Podcrash",
  "pack.name": "ARCHAEOLOGY Add-On",
  "pod_arch.button.back": "Back",
  "pod_arch.button.exit": "Exit",
  "pod_arch.display_stand.all_bones_added": "§cYou've already added all bones of this type to the Display Stand!",
  "pod_arch.display_stand.needs_assembling": "§cThis bone cannot directly go onto the Display Stand!%1You need to assemble it to a bigger part of the skeleton first using an Assembly Table.",
  "pod_arch.display_stand.no_space": "§cThere is not enough space for this display stand here!",
  "pod_arch.display_stand.obstructed": "§cThis display stand was obstructed!",
  "pod_arch.display_stand.unidentified_bone": "§cIdentify this bone first using an Identification Table before putting it on a display stand!",
  "pod_arch.display_stand.wrong_mob": "§cThis bone does not belong to the mob displayed on this Display Stand!",
  "pod_arch.dungeon.enter": "§pYou have entered a temple and have been cursed with mining fatigue!",
  "pod_arch.guide.body": "§o§7Created by Podcrash§r%1%1Ready for an adventure? The ARCHAEOLOGY Add-On brings new custom chiseling and brushing mechanics to your world! Unearth ancient artifacts from the grounds, collect different types of pottery, and craft rare talismans that will provide great buffs! Find bones from long-dead mobs, wash and identify them, and try to complete all of the 47 different Skeleton Display Stands! Discover 30+ unique new structures to your world with lootable chests, custom traps, and fun challenges! Lost your book? Craft a new one using a book and a bone!.%1%1For help and guidance, check out §3§ohttps://pdcr.sh/archaeology§r",
  "pod_arch.guide.bones.assemblies": "The following bones can be assembled:",
  "pod_arch.guide.bones.body": "While Chiseling & Brushing, you can find Piles of Bones. These are dirty and hard to identify. You need to take them to a washing station to clean them. After you've washed the bones, you can identify them at an identification table. Finally, you need to assemble some of the bones on an Assembly Table before you can put them on a Display Stand. On this page, we will work you through doing that.%1%1§lWashing Station§r%1First, bring your piles of bones that you have found while excavating to a washing station. After placing the washing station, ensure it is filled with water so that the bones can be cleaned properly. Then, click the washing station with the pile of bones to put them in, and it will take a bit to wash them. Be aware that during this process, there is a risk of the bones breaking. Once the bones are clean, you can remove them again by clicking on the block. Now, you should be good to take the bones you've found to an identification table. You can craft a washing station by putting a cauldron in the middle slot of your crafting table grid. Then, put planks on both sides of the cauldron, and finally, fill the row below the cauldron with planks, too!%1%1§lIdentification Table§r%1Next, take the unidentified bones you have just washed to the identification table and click it with a bone to identify the bone; this takes a few seconds, but nothing can go wrong! After you have identified a bone, you can either display it directly on a stand or assemble it with a larger part of a skeleton first. You can look up what to do with the bone on the mob's page, which is listed on this page. To craft an identification table, place a spyglass in the centre of your crafting table grid and fully surround it with planks.%1%1§lAssembly Table§r%1Some of the bones found need to be combined into a bigger part of a skeleton first before it can be put onto the display stand. To do so, bring the parts of the skeleton to the Assembly Table. You can look up which bones you need to combine directly in the assembly table or on the mob's page that is listed on this page. To craft the Assembly Table, fill the top row of a crafting table grid with iron ingots. In the center slot of the grid, put a chisel. Finally, fill the remaining slots with planks.%1%1§lDisplay Stands§r%1All creatures listed below can be displayed on Display Stands! Place a display stand and then click it with a bone to add the bone to the display stand. On the page of the creature in this menu, you can find how many bones of which kind you need to fully assemble a mob on a display stand. Can you collect them all? To craft a display stand, put a stick in the center slot of a crafting table grid, then fill the row below it with smooth stone slabs.",
  "pod_arch.guide.bones.bone_with_quantity": "%1x %2",
  "pod_arch.guide.bones.display_stand": "The following bones can be put onto a display stand:",
  "pod_arch.guide.bones.excavation": "The following bones from %1 can be found from excavating:",
  "pod_arch.guide.bones.title": "Bones & Processing",
  "pod_arch.guide.chiseling.body": "Using a Chisel or a Brush, you can uncover ancient artifacts from different blocks that would usually break when mining the block. Right-click the block with a chisel or a brush to start excavating!%1%1To craft a brush, put a stick in the bottom left corner of a crafting table grid. In the middle slot of the grid, put a piece of leather. In the top right slot, put an iron ingot, and your chisel will be done! For brushing, you can use the vanilla brush item.%1%1Chiseling works in all horizontal directions as well as downwards. The following blocks can be chiseled:%1Stone, Andesite, Diorite, Granite, Tuff, Deepslate, Sandstone, Red Sandstone, Hardened Clay, and all types of Terracotta.%1%1Brushing only works downwards. The following blocks can be brushed:%1Grass Block, Dirt, Gravel, Sand, Red Sand.%1%1There is a chance to find different ancient artifacts when chiseling or brushing a block within it. The following artifacts can be found:%1Skystriped Vase, Twinhandled Jar, Story Pot, Painted Pot, Obsidian Cask, Moss Jar, Herald Pot, Ember Pot, Band Pot, Pile of Bones, and various Items.",
  "pod_arch.guide.chiseling.title": "Chiseling & Brushing",
  "pod_arch.guide.structures.body": "The 30+ new Structures added by this Add-On deliver new and exciting elements for every player. There are two types of structures, Ruins and Temples. Ruins can be found more frequently and usually contain a few loot chests and mob spawners. They are often partly or wholly buried, and you have to excavate them to fully explore them! On the other hand, there are the Temples, which are packed with traps and other challenges but provide better loot than the ruins. Depending on the biome you are in, there are various different structures that you can find.",
  "pod_arch.guide.structures.title": "Structures",
  "pod_arch.guide.talisman.body": "Talisman can be crafted from talisman shards and will supply buffs to the player while being carried in the inventory. Talisman shards can be found in custom structures and from chiseling & brushing. You can then combine 8 talisman shards with the item of the effect you want the talisman to give. The talisman will lose durability over time, but you can repair it again using talisman shards in an anvil. The following talisman types exist: %1%1§lTalisman of Night Vision§r%1Crafted using a golden carrot.%1Gives Night Vision I.%1%1§lTalisman of Haste§r%1Crafted using a diamond pickaxe.%1Gives Haste I.%1%1§lTalisman of Speed§r%1Crafted using sugar.%1Gives Speed I.%1%1§lTalisman of Jump Boost§r%1Crafted using a rabbit's foot.%1Gives Jump Boost I.%1%1§lTalisman of Fire Resistance§r%1Crafted using magma cream.%1Gives Fire Resistance I.%1%1§lTalisman of Regeneration§r%1Crafted using a ghast tear.%1Gives Regeneration I.%1%1§lTalisman of Resistance§r%1Crafted using turtle scute.%1Gives Resistance I.%1%1§lTalisman of Strength§r%1Crafted using blaze powder.%1Gives Strength I.%1%1§lTalisman of Slow Falling§r%1Crafted using Phantom Membrane.%1Gives Slow Falling I.%1%1§lTalisman of Water Breathing§r%1Crafted using a pufferfish.%1Givves Water Breathing I.",
  "pod_arch.guide.talisman.title": "Talisman",
  "pod_arch.guide.title": "ARCHAEOLOGY Add-On",
  "pod_arch.guide.translate.body": "We try to support as many languages as we can. Our Add-On currently supports:\\n\\n- English\\n- French\\n- German\\n- Indonesian\\n- Italian\\n- Japanese\\n- Korean\\n- Polish\\n- Portuguese (PT/BR)\\n- Spanish (ES/MX)\\n\\nIf you find an issue, or if we're missing your language, help us improve our translations at §o§shttps://pdcr.sh/translate§r",
  "pod_arch.guide.translate.title": "Translate",
  "pod_arch.guide.traps.body": "The temples added by this Add-On are filled with a bunch of unique traps. Along with traps built with redstone, a few custom traps have been added.%1%1§lSpike Trap§r%1The spike trap can be placed in any direction. It must be triggered by redstone from behind. Mobs and Players that are standing on the spike trap will receive high amounts of damage. A Spike Trap can be crafted by filling the top row of a crafting table grid with iron bars and then putting a piston in the middle slot of the crafting table. Finally, fill all other slots up with cobblestone.%1%1§lSwinging Axe§r%1The swinging axe is a deadly trap that can be placed on ceilings. A large axe will hang down; once the top of the swinging axe is powered by redstone, the axe will start swinging, knocking away any player or mob in its way. It can be crafted by putting an iron block in the top middle slot of a crafting table grid. Then, you need to put planks on both sides of the iron block. Below the iron block, put an iron axe. Finally, also put planks on both sides of the iron axe.%1%1§lRolling Boulder Trap§r%1The rolling boulder is held by a little piece of wood. Once the block receives power, the boulder will be released and roll in the direction it was placed, squashing any player or mob in its way. The boulder will break when colliding with a wall. The Rolling Boulder Trap can be crafted by putting a piston in the bottom left corner of the crafting table grid. Then, put an iron ingot in the middle slot of the crafting table grid. Finally, fill the remaining slots around the iron with cobblestone.%1%1§lStone Golem§r%1Stone Golems have been sleeping in temples for thousands of years. Watch out; when you step too close to them, you may wake them up. They are strong and tanky mobs that will protect the temple at any cost. The Stone Golem can only be found in temples and not crafted or obtained in any way.%1%1§lHeart of the Dungeon§r%1The heart of the dungeon protects temples from intruders. It will apply mining fatigue to all players that enter a temple area. The heart of the dungeon can be broken to disable it. It is not obtainable for the player and can only be found in temples.",
  "pod_arch.guide.traps.title": "Traps",
  "pod_arch.washing_station.bones_break": "§cThe bones broke during the washing process!",
  "pod_arch.washing_station.filled": "§cPlease wait until the station is finished washing the bones!",
  "pod_arch.washing_station.no_water": "§cPlease add water using a water bucket first to proceed!",
